ype":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When identity and authority backends are not admitted, Control API callers need an explicit unavailable boundary. Add a pure, no-argument WSGI app: only constant public capability metadata succeeds, protected reads return unavailable, and mutation routes deny. No listener, provider/backend injection, request-body reads, clock or network/system I/O. Only four allocated new files change; existing/shared files remain untouched.\n\nThe explicit unified.control-error.p0.v1 profile has null request identity and is intentionally incompatible with frozen Terminan Sync v1. No startup wiring, operator provider, actual snapshot/event/receipt backend or consensus implementation is introduced. Strict-time, closure/allocation and dispatch-containment gates remain closed.\n\nBase: mission/operator-control-plane @ 2df6f5c2f77f4d883bad1a8623dd8375db529be0 (tree f10c13d2dd8a2a88fd7db9a4cf0d0e7a1cd6d0d4). HEAD: 320b5d0894019d72aa8927dc5c4246d28c6e5f3c; tree 7c69196e55afd314e4547d327cf5e1d45eb43d94. Ownership revision3 and immutable P0 profile e4b7f009e6f81cc5baa46be604abde8edd05cc6f48dfb5ac711879343c49d20c bound in documentation.\n\nValidation: 16 focused Python3.12 tests PASS, zero skips; full local Python3.12 suite 724 tests, zero failures/errors, 14 explicit baseline skips (privilege and missing cross-repository fixtures). Diagnostic pre-change Python3.15 baseline: 708 tests, zero failures, 14 skips; not supported dependency qualification. Independent review found a HEAD response-body defect, fixed with red/green regression tests and re-reviewed. Dedicated Ubuntu/Windows Python3.11/3.12 CI records exact HEAD/tree and rejects skipped focused cases; hosted status must be checked separately.\n\nThis PR is P0 component evidence only. Runtime Control API, Windows identity, real consensus/fencing/failover and physical HA remain NOT_QUALIFIED / NO-GO. No merge, deployment or physical tests authorized.","labels":[],"mileston